# 11. TREATMENT APPLICATION AND RECORDING

Separate the treatment that the application recommends from the treatment the user actually applies.

Users must be able to confirm, modify, or decline a recommendation.

When a user records a treatment, capture:

- Plant identifier.
- Treatment identifier.
- Application date and time.
- Product or ingredients.
- Actual quantity applied.
- Dilution or preparation details.
- Application method.
- Reason for treatment.
- Cost where known.
- User notes.
- Supporting photograph where appropriate.
- Expected follow-up date.

Do not automatically mark a treatment as applied merely because it was recommended.

Allow users to record partial applications, skipped treatments, or changes made during application.

Keep a dated history of treatment changes and outcomes.

